## 3. Notes
- It reads the page and never changes it. The blueprint is drawn on a canvas from the elements on screen when the lights go out, and again when you scroll.
- Holding on a link, button or form field does nothing, so clicks and typing still work normally.
- The letter construction works on `h1`, `h2`, `h3` and anything with a `data-construct` attribute, if its font is `MIN_SIZE` (22px) or bigger. Add `data-construct` to other big text you want it on. `LIFT` sets how far the letters move.
- While a heading is hovered, its real text is made transparent and the same letters are drawn on the canvas so they can move. Nothing in the page's DOM is moved or rewritten, and the text comes back the moment the cursor leaves.
- Headings that already animate their own text are left alone: clipped or masked text (like the dot-matrix "I'M YOUR PERSON" heading while it wipes in), rotated or vertical text, and text whose ink is invisible. Add `data-no-construct` to any other element you want it to skip. Headings under an open overlay (the full-screen build, the contact overlay) don't react either.
- When several headings are stacked in one place (like the build captions, where only one is visible at a time), it picks the one that is actually visible.
- A small hint, "Hold anywhere to see how it's built", appears once, about 3.5 seconds after the first visit, and never again after the visitor has tried it.

